<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    iOS alert / action-sheet surface.

    iOS alerts are a floating rounded card, not a full-width sheet. Radius is
    14dp, which is the platform dialog_corner_radius AppleUX ships in
    appleux/rro-frameworks/res/values/dimens.xml and in
    FrameworkOverlayRock/res/values/dimens.xml — all three now read 14dp so
    every dialog in the OS draws the same curve.

    Fill and hairline stroke come from the grouped-background and opaque
    separator tokens so the alert tracks light/dark without a second shape.

    Deliberately NOT a translucent gradient: `?android:attr/windowIsTranslucent`
    plus a real blur costs a full-screen render pass behind every dialog. On a
    4 GB device the flat card is both cheaper and closer to iOS 27, which only
    blurs when the presentation warrants it.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@color/secondary_system_grouped_background" />
    <stroke
        android:width="0.5dp"
        android:color="@color/separator_primary" />
    <corners android:radius="14dp" />
</shape>